## Windows stack alignment and CI disk usage — 2026-10-23T06:54:16Z

Remote GitHub run `39730752050` at `662d98c5` showed the native Windows
stack-capture regression failing: `jstack-worker` was listed but its next line
was `<native stack unavailable>`. The windows-sys `CONTEXT` layout lacks the
16-byte native alignment needed by Windows x64 `GetThreadContext`; see the
Microsoft Windows SDK alignment requirement in the
[GetThreadContext documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/processthreadsapi/nf-processthreadsapi-getthreadcontext)
and the upstream [windows-rs metadata issue](https://github.com/microsoft/win32metadata/issues/1477).
Commit `f375e3f0` wraps the context in `#[repr(C, align(16))]` storage on both
x64 and ARM64 before capture and unwinding. Native macOS stack regression:
1 passed. Full Windows GNU workspace check across all targets and features:
passed. A focused ARM64/MSVC compile of the context and unwind calls passed.
The full ARM64/MSVC workspace check is unavailable on this Mac because the
Windows ARM64 C toolchain and standard headers required by aws-lc-sys and
zstd-sys are absent.

The same remote Ubuntu run failed while linking the Remoting security target
with `No space left on device` after Clippy and workspace tests had produced
large debug artifacts. Commit `7a4f132e` sets Cargo dev/test debug information
to zero and disables incremental compilation in the Ubuntu CI job. With the
reduced test profile, all seven Remoting security integration tests passed
locally. The amended GitHub job was not run or pushed.

Before these Windows-only and workflow commits, Linux ARM64 revision
`73721ae5` passed the server-free refresh: formatting, strict all-target/all-
feature Clippy, default and all-feature workspace tests, the Asia/Taipei unique
ID fixture, differential self-test and 37-scenario manifest, fuzz smoke (163
frame seeds, 11 message seeds, 2,784 bounded mutations, 245 frame decodes,
192 message decodes), 17 deterministic race/leak cases × 3, release examples,
benchmark compilation, and workspace metadata. After `f375e3f0`, the focused
native macOS stack regression and full Windows GNU cross-check passed.

No external CI run or push was performed. Current-revision GitHub
