## P18-V01 MQClientAPIFactory nullable callback and discovery parity — 2026-10-23T09:13:51Z

Pinned Java `MQClientAPIFactory.onNameServerAddressChange(null)` delegates to
each API client, where null leaves the current address unchanged. Before
startup, the same call fails because the factory client array is null. Rust
now preserves both boundaries with its typed not-started error and Java-null
no-op. The factory also ignores blank `TopAddressing` results like Java's
`MQClientAPIImpl.fetchNameServerAddr`/`UtilAll.isBlank`; direct callback strings
remain unfiltered. Commit `805619a9` records the code and expanded fixture.

